  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing differences between outcomes and a reference value (zero in this case), then evaluating the expected value of those differences (i.e., expected monetary value), and preferring the lottery with the more favorable mean difference. In this case, both lotteries have the same expected value (1500), so the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not compute or reference such differences or expected values. Instead, the individual focuses on the probability of winning any money (50% vs. 25%) and expresses a preference for having any gain over having none. This is a different reasoning process — one based on the probability of a positive outcome, not on expected differences from a reference value. Therefore, the individual did not use the specified decision reason. The reported justification does not involve differences from a reference value or their weighted mean. It instead relies on a different criterion (probability of winning). Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
